<Page
    x:Class="MbcsCentral.Help.EmailOverview"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
    xmlns:local="clr-namespace:MbcsCentral.Help"
    xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
    Title="EmailOverview"
    d:DesignHeight="636.031"
    mc:Ignorable="d">
    <Page.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
                <ResourceDictionary Source="HelpStyles.xaml" />
            </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        </ResourceDictionary>
    </Page.Resources>

    <Grid>
        <ScrollViewer 
            Width="Auto" 
            Height="643" 
            VerticalAlignment="Top" 
            VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" 
            CanContentScroll="True">
            <StackPanel 
                Height="640" 
                HorizontalAlignment="Left" 
                VerticalAlignment="Top">
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HeaderText}">Email Overview</TextBlock>
                <Separator />
                <TextBlock 
                    Width="Auto"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                    TextWrapping="Wrap">
                    The ability to E-Mail has been incorporated into several functions:
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource InnerText}">                    
                    1.	Directly to Tenants (WinPM)
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource IndentedInnerText}">
                    You can choose any E-Mail address from the tenant record.  You type the subject and message. 
                    You can optionally include an attachment that is either a file on your system or scanned directly to the message.
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource InnerText}">
                    2.	Late Notices (WinPM)
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource IndentedInnerText}">
                    In addition to printing Late Notices for hand or regular mail distribution, they can be processed and immediately sent 
                    via E-Mail to any address in the tenant record.  The Notice is sent as an attachment and looks the same as the printed version.
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource InnerText}">
                    3.	Reports, individual (WinPM, WinGL)
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource IndentedInnerText}">
                    All reports can be emailed to one or more recipients from the Report Display window.  Recipients can be pulled from 
                    Outlook Contacts, personalized recipient lists, or added one at a time.
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource InnerText}">
                    4.	Batch Reports (WinGL)
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource IndentedInnerText}">
                    This is similar to E-Mailing individual reports except that an entire batch is sent at one time to all recipients.
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock>
                    <LineBreak/>
                    There are different user interfaces depending on which of the functions you use.  But whichever one you use, you must first set up the E-Mail account(s) through which you will be sending the messages.
                </TextBlock>
                        
            </StackPanel>
        </ScrollViewer>
    </Grid>
</Page>
